{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness","id":1094075,"title":"What would be Your new World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-18T04:42:00-07:00","id":1094075,"title":"What would be Your new World of Darkness?","content":"V5 is comming. There are lot of topics here about edge, WWP decisions and other things. I've read a lot of fantastic discussions between WoD fans here and I've learned that most yo You have a lot of very interesting ideas, I'd love to read about. So if You would be a lead designer of V5, WtA5 and other what would be Your main metaplot, how would You change the WoD, expand it?<br /> <br /> I'll make an example. Wars in Africa and big migration. What would stay behind it in WoD? Would it be because of new impegrium? Or would it be some distraction from powerful vampires true goals? Lot of options..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:00:00-07:00","id":1094129,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't have changed the rules in such drastic ways, I would have focused in refining them, and into making a general rulebook about common stuff (like CoD rules for humans, weapons and stuff). <br /> <br /> Let's try to make the games more crossover friendly, without reducing it to the, let's say, homogeneity, of CoD. Having common rules being...well...common (and not like 20th where a Katana does different damages in each rulebook) it's a start. Balance isn't important, but keeping to the themes of the games is.<br /> <br /> Maybe what I'm saying it's that I WOULDN'T make a New WoD, because this it's marketed as a &quot;new edition&quot;, but by now everyone knows that isn't a new edition of classic WoD, but, as you say, it's a new WoD. It is a remake, a series of new games that keeps the continuity of previous cWoD games to exploit their old clients.<br /> <br /> Advancing the Metaplot it's a tall order after the &quot;end of the world&quot;, but I don't think the approach they've taken it's bad.<br /> I wouldn't have put the Anarchy over the Camarilla so easily. I think the Camarilla it's better prepared to take the offensive of Technocrats/world goverments that is the new inquisition.<br /> I also wouldn't have made a new Inquisition, per se, but rather a sort of Compact. Some big mortal world goverments and powers know a little about the horrors that lurk in the dark, but precisely because they don't know the extense of the supernatural &quot;problem&quot;, they aren't about to start a secret war against vampires, but rather they have pursued, and eventually reached an understanding with the various supernatural powers, that goes more or less like &quot;you keep your busines secret and I cooperate to hide evidence instead of going out of my way to kill you all&quot;. Which it's a plan that the Technocracy can get behind because they &quot;know&quot; (no matter if they're right or not) that the supernatural will e eradicated when they control the Consensus, while Pentex will beneffit of the keeping of the status quo, and have the resources of the mortal goverment to cleanse any fomori incident under the assumtion that they're just roge supernaturals unafiliated with any major group.<br /> Shady figures in the goverment, mafia, and big business may have both the mundane and supernatural (thanks to pentex or technocracy) resources needed to actually make deals with vampires and others from a possition of power, but this wouldn't be common. <br /> Antediluvians are awake but they are so inteligent and capable that their war and actions can only be perceived by minor supernaturals as big shifts of the Jyhad board, of whom the &quot;calling&quot; of the Sabbat to the east can be one of said moves.<br /> Ascencion didn't happened, obviously, though maybe the meteor thing did happened and was averted successfully. I would keep the events as in the Technocracy Convention books + M20.<br /> Don't know enough about Werewolf to develop a clever way arround the Apocalipse not destroying the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:13:50-07:00","id":1094136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1094129#post1094129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Don't know enough about Werewolf to develop a clever way arround the Apocalipse not destroying the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf's last metaplot events were geared up for the end years before Apocalypse came out, since Garou and Fera had experienced a complete cutoff of new births (lots of kin, no changers) and there was a certain message of &quot;everyone who is going to participate in the Apocalypse has already been born.&quot;<br /> <br /> You'd have to roll back events considerably or outright ignore them. There's no clever way of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:20:23-07:00","id":1094174,"title":"","content":"Or let garou win the battle but not the war. Making apocalypse not the one final battle but final age or ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:43:46-07:00","id":1094246,"title":"","content":"I actually like how BNS: WtA handled the specifics of moving the metaplot forward. The battles at the end of Revised turned out to be the start of a whole new age (which actually fits with a few things in the larger WoD) and the face of the war has changed after Gaia did something that caused her to wane significantly in power but revitalized the werefolk and their kin significantly in the process.<br /> <br /> All in all though, if I was in charge of the new edition, the metaplot would be my last concern. The metaplot is a problem at this point - and one that doesn't have to be solved to keep the fans happy - because the core play experience of almost 15 years of the WoD was that the End was coming. Once the End has come... the games have to become something different.<br /> <br /> My primary focus would be on mechanics. The 20th books were great collections, and some had some much needed cleaning up in them, but the games could use a major overhaul on the rules, and greater standardization. I don't think you need to make the mechanics more CofD-like to be &quot;21st Century&quot; in design. D&amp;D 5e feels like a modern game without making major changes to the play style D&amp;D focuses on. I love the CofD games, I have them when I want to play them. When I want to play a WoD game, I want to play a WoD game, not a CofD game with the WoD setting (not that this isn't appealing to people to, but it shouldn't be the focus of designing a new WoD edition).<br /> <br /> When it comes to the plot, I'd do something very different. I'd pick a date. 2000, 2012, something. This becomes &quot;year 0.&quot; All core books and major supplements consider year 0 the base-line. Then we get to do metaplot<b>s</b>. People that don't care about the metaplot have a solid core game to play with and do what they will. Each game line can have their own focused metaplot, as well as one universal metaplot, and maybe even crossover ones between a few lines. All such things would be labelled clearly. The metaplot series supplements become massive modules to enjoy. And if one reaches a logical conclusion... well just start a new one!<br /> <br /> This lets the creative team endlessly explore the games by looking at different ways the metaplot can go. It also makes handling things like transmedia and participatory engagement easier. The universal metaplot gets to be the &quot;One WOD&quot; that everything goes into, while the smaller line-based metaplots are unaffected, or have more focused participatory inputs. Players can choose to be in the One WOD where a major Masquerade breech gets the Technocracy up in arms and they crack down on Changelings nearby, or they can choose to be in purely WtA focused metaplot games where only WtA focused events will influence the official metaplot for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T05:59:20-07:00","id":1141035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1094129#post1094129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have put the Anarchy over the Camarilla so easily. I think the Camarilla it's better prepared to take the offensive of Technocrats/world goverments that is the new inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this 'new inquisition' at all supported by the Technocracy? It's not really the 'world governments', isn't it? More like groups of politicians, policemen, government workers, and secret service agents.<br /> <br /> Where can I read more about this 'new inquisition'?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1094129#post1094129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) but rather they have pursued, and eventually reached an understanding with the various supernatural powers, that goes more or less like &quot;you keep your busines secret and I cooperate to hide evidence instead of going out of my way to kill you all&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How could they make such an agreement if they are in no position to make real the &quot;kill you all&quot; part?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1094129#post1094129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shady figures in the goverment, mafia, and big business may have both the mundane and supernatural (thanks to pentex or technocracy) resources needed to actually make deals with vampires and others from a possition of power, but this wouldn't be common.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like the usual manipulations and actions of the Technocracy (maybe unusual if they are actually providing Technocratic technology to those wholly uninitiated) and the usual actions undertaken by Pentex. What would make this 'new inquisition' or 'Compact' any different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T16:32:33-07:00","id":1141249,"title":"","content":"I don't believe RPG games should have metaplot. I want a compelling setting with lots of potential conflicts that can be explored, but I don't want or need someone to be a Master Storyteller telling me how to run my games. What I want are toolkits that allow me to run the games I want to run myself. I certainly don't want something where the people I am giving money too now tells me that what I am doing is &quot;wrong&quot; in someway.<br /> <br /> So setting up the general Camarilla vs Sabbat conflict is fine. I can take it from there. I don't want someone telling me that the setting has now changed because this city or that has fallen. Nor is telling me that if I am running a game where the primary conflict is Camarilla vs Anarch, and the Sabbat is in the background, that the game now says the Camarilla-Anarch conflict is moot because the Sabbat is the primary enemy. Or any other changes.<br /> <br /> If someone has a really great idea of how to portray a Camarilla Sabbat conflict and wants to produce material for it. That is great. But it shouldn't be &quot;metaplot.&quot; It should be in the format of a By Night book where a brand new city is portrayed, and then set up the details for that city alone so that an ST can run it for the PCs if they want. That way STs (and PCs) have specific examples and can see how things can play out instead of very vague ideas that never make the connections. STs can then run the city as is. Or transplant it into a new city and run it. Or just pillage it for cool ideas and NPCs.<br /> <br /> Metaplot for me ruins great RPG settings. And it has gotten me to not buy new sourcebook material or even abandon the setting or gameline. It doesn't matter if it is D&amp;D, World of Darkness, or something else.<br /> <br /> I would have no objection to a book that lays out several possible &quot;metaplots&quot; that STs may want to use (similar to how the final books of each game line were presented). So present a scenario like the one in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and then another how it was in Revised. And the one where the Anarchs have won another great victory and shows the Loyalist Sabbat leaving their sect to join the new Anarchs. Or whatever plot it is. Use them to give the STs new tools on how they can each kind of game, and how the mysteries of the setting are changed in the different campaign types. That way even if an ST doesn't use any of the plots, they'll still have new toolkits to use and see how different kind of games can result from the basic setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T21:00:23-07:00","id":1141301,"title":"","content":"I don't think metaplot is always bad. But it's best when it's used sparingly. Shadowrun, for example, has always had a metaplot, but as a cyberpunk setting, the advancing of time in the default setting also means being able to update the technology of the setting to keep people that don't want to be retro all the time more interested. The metaplot happened (not always perfectly of course) pulled back from what most PCs would be doing. Megacorps could rise and fall, but Runners don't have to care because there's always Corps looking for their services. Putting the focus on play on people outside the system, the metaplot focused on how the system changes reduces the &quot;Master Storyteller&quot; issues the WoD metaplot frequently suffered.<br /> <br /> Metaplot is problematic for the WoD, because it focused on things that directly impact the default modes of play, and the way the WoD is structured to allow a wide variety of modes of play, there's no &quot;place&quot; to focus the metaplot where that stops happening. Players can become movers and shakers in the Camarilla, so you can't just focus the metaplot on the Cam leadership without intruding. Sure, I can run an apprentice Mage game, and ignore the metaplot fairly easily. But when PCs start being Adepts and Masters.. the metaplot gets right in their face.<br /> <br /> So, to an extent, metaplot needs to be part of the game play expectations from the get go. If you design for it, you can make sure you leave space for it. But once the game is set up without that room, adding it is hard to do well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T07:15:20-07:00","id":1141397,"title":"","content":"<i>If </i> I had the choice, i will going more of the taste of the first edition for vampire, a game more about personnal horror and the way to lose your humanity than affronting war ghouls with Katana\u2122. you can have action and aventure but more in a street level. I want to have some ghouls sect i can use, some strnage rumors to hear about and some very alien elders to fight. <br /> And i 'm writing a ton of context based supplement, i want more by night more rage accross, more descriptions of theme , locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15012-niico","name":"Niico","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15012_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:28:57-07:00","id":1141433,"title":"","content":"Personally I like metaplot not only does it lead to some interesting changes to the setting (even if I don't always like all of them) it provides sources for new ideas. In general I tended to take most of the metaplot with only a few shifts here and there to match the setting I wanted to portray. Generally the only metaplot points (outside of those presented in the endline books Gehenna, Apocalypse, Ascension, and Time of Judgement) I consistently ignored were [Ravnos] awakening causing the near annihilation of the Ravnos clan; the destruction of Stygia, and the Avatar Storm. Even then I usually tweaked or altered them to be a similar but lesser event a Ravnos elder/methuselah awakening and going on a frenzy bender or a storm across the gauntlet that was more temporary but still disruptive.<br /> <br /> As for what my WoD would like like.<ul><li>Better crossover rules and consistency. I like using different supernaturals and playing them off each other and I would like the rules to be clearer how to do that.<ul><li>Spirits, Wraiths, Demons, Elementals, Umbrood and the like would be clarified by setting the rules based on the origin of the entity as follows.<ul><li>Elemental: Spirits related to objects, concepts, and places. Most umbrood (outside of angels/demons) are going to fall into this category including Werewolf Totems, Banes, other Wyrm Spirits, and Tenebrous entities (what would be called Abyssal like Obtenebration's Abyss Mysticism, but I would separate the pre-light darkness from the prison of demons).</li> <li>Wraiths: Spirits of the dead and the underworld including Spectres, Risen, and the Neverborn.</li> <li>Supernal/Infernal: Angels, Demons, and the Kuei-jin (even though they were people their time in Yomi along with the second breath has altered them into something different from a Wraith) fall into this category</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>More material for running game lines in different eras. Vampire: The Dark Ages was my first WW RPG and I have loved the setting ever since. The further Dark Ages books were all interesting interpretations of those lines. I also think that Dark Ages had some of the best setting supplements like Transylvania by Night, Veil of Night, Dark Ages British Isles, and Dark Ages Europe.<ul><li>For each I would like to see a book along the lines of Dark Ages British Isles and Dark Ages Europe with a brief overview of important areas, mortals, and supernaturals with the addition of specific rules/creation guidelines for the supernaturals of that era.</li> <li>As for what time periods I would like to see, the more the better. The following are ones that I think would make some of the best break points (and some have already been used by WW): Ancient (Mesopotamian city states, early Egypt, Mediterranean city states, essentially everything pre-Rome), Rome, Dark Ages, Renaissance, Colonial, Victorian (up to WWI), WW2, Cold War<ul><li>Of those I think Ancient, Rome, and WW2 are the ones I would like to see most that haven't been done in some way in the current WW lines.</li> <li>Each era book would also offer insight in to how changes to canon history within them might affect future eras like if Carthage weren't destroyed by Rome, or if the Camarilla never formed, essentially a brief what if section</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:44:49-07:00","id":1141441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141035#post1141035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this 'new inquisition' at all supported by the Technocracy? It's not really the 'world governments', isn't it? More like groups of politicians, policemen, government workers, and secret service agents.<br /> <br /> Where can I read more about this 'new inquisition'?</div> </div> </div> </div>From now we have only rumors. I'm not aware of more sources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not really the 'world governments', isn't it? </div> </div> </div>Maybe that isn't the case, but I understood that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How could they make such an agreement if they are in no position to make real the &quot;kill you all&quot; part? </div> </div> </div>The Masquerade doesn't exist for shit and giggles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> This sounds like the usual manipulations and actions of the Technocracy (maybe unusual if they are actually providing Technocratic technology to those wholly uninitiated) and the usual actions undertaken by Pentex. What would make this 'new inquisition' or 'Compact' any different? </div> </div> </div>It would be different because A, they're humans, a lot of them, the real movers and shakers of a world that's primarily controled by humans. and B, they're hunters. The Inquisition it's why The Masquerade exists, why mages abide to the same rule, so a &quot;new Inquisition&quot; that has more resources, conections, and technology to it's exectution than old christian church could hope to put in motion it's serious business for everyone even if it doesn't eliminate whole splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-18-2017, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:30:37-07:00","id":1141683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141441#post1141441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Masquerade doesn't exist for shit and giggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does the existence of the Masquerade relate to the supposed capability of this new inquisition to &quot;kill all supernaturals&quot; ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141441#post1141441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be different because A, they're humans, a lot of them,</div> </div> </div> </div>How many?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141441#post1141441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the real movers and shakers of a world that's primarily controled by humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked the world, if primarily controlled by anyone, is primarily controlled by Kindred Methuselahs, Kindred Elders, and True Mages groups - and perhaps other Nightfolk. (I don't know about the Fera, for example.) What makes a mundane businessmen or a politician capable at all to be a 'mover and shaker' compared to the Nightfolk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141441#post1141441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and B, they're hunters. The Inquisition it's why The Masquerade exists, why mages abide to the same rule, so a &quot;new Inquisition&quot; that has more resources, conections, and technology to it's exectution than old christian church could hope to put in motion it's serious business for everyone even if it doesn't eliminate whole splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they motivated by religion?<br /> <br /> The problem with trying to do a new inquisition is that the Masquerade exists. Hence a person is going to have a hard time convincing anyone of the existence of the Kindred - not to mention stuff like the varied Discipline capabilities or the existence of Kindred Ghouls.<br /> Another big problem is that the Technocracy - and not only them - has effectively enforced a secular, non-supernatural outlook and point of view on the masses of humanity. This makes it hard to recruit new members; and can also make it hard to actually make moves against the supernaturals as a group of mundane persons.<br /> For example - a stack of notes on the supernatural made by someone is enough to discredit them if it is publicized.<br /> Another one - the fact that mundane humans might become totally estranged and isolated from their loved ones and friends; because even if they attempt to tell them about the supernatural, they very often will meet with total disbelief. A person not coming back home increasingly often does not look good for a spouse or a best friend. Such a disrupted social life can of course be exploited by the Nightfolk. If they try to make up the lost time to their families and friends, then the new inquisition loses capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-19-2017, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T09:20:58-07:00","id":1141777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1094075-what-would-be-your-new-world-of-darkness?p=1141683#post1141683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the existence of the Masquerade relate to the supposed capability of this new inquisition to &quot;kill all supernaturals&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked: How could they make such an agreement if they are in no position to make real the &quot;kill you all&quot; part?<br /> <br /> That agreement it's already in place without Goverments doing anything, it's called &quot;The Masquerade&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it's in place because the Inquisition was dangerous to Elders. If vampires could rule the world openly, like Tzimisce did in Transilvania, they would do it. But they can't. Vampires fear what humanity could do, that's why even the Sabbat respects the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Thus, the existence of the Masquerade matters: If the powers that be in the human world were to politely ask Elders to keep doing <i>what they're already doing to survive</i> (to keep their businees secret and clean), I imagine Elders would have little problem to comply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last time I checked the world, if primarily controlled by anyone, is primarily controlled by Kindred Methuselahs, Kindred Elders, and True Mages groups - and perhaps other Nightfolk. (I don't know about the Fera, for example.) </div> </div> </div>It seems that you missed revised edition. You can't Ghoul the president anymore, it's a risk to the Masquerade. Masquerade breaches are dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What makes a mundane businessmen or a politician capable at all to be a 'mover and shaker' compared to the Nightfolk? </div> </div> </div>Free time. They aren't in a shadow war with other powers nor have interests in the Occult (that takes time).<br /> <br /> It's funny how people makes &quot;social control&quot; a superpower. Vampires control the world without opposition, it doesn't matter how, they just do. If the prince calls, US army has to go to the city and blow up whatever the prince wants to blow up.<br /> <br /> Vampires are 24/7 cheking with the hundreds of blood bound thralls they would need to control everything unchallenged and undiscovered, and they still have time to develop Disciplines, study Occult, fend from their numerous enemies, sleep, hunt (yeah, it's surprising how many &quot;lords of the night&quot; hunt or tend a flock, like peasants. Why don't they just ask the police to bring them people to suck dry, if they control everything?), and of course, they do so without opposition.<br /> <br /> The subtle difference between control and influence it's that influence it's far subtler and takes much less time: You can have a Ghoul in a key place, he alone doesn't control what happens in that place, but he can nudge what happens to your benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with trying to do a new inquisition is that the Masquerade exists </div> </div> </div>And that's why I'm critic of a new Inquisition, it presumes governments know too much. It's the most important Masquerade breach since it's inception, Nightfolk have means to prevent this, did they even try?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> .<br /> Hence a person is going to have a hard time convincing anyone of the existence of the Kindred - not to mention stuff like the varied Discipline capabilities or the existence of Kindred Ghouls. </div> </div> </div>This is not a problem, the old Inquisition used the real inquisition as a cover, nothing more: Kings and armies weren't &quot;in the know&quot;, only certain authorities of the church knew about the true nature of the supernatural. People doesn't need to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another big problem is that the Technocracy - and not only them - has effectively enforced a secular, non-supernatural outlook and point of view on the masses of humanity. This makes it hard to recruit new members; and can also make it hard to actually make moves against the supernaturals as a group of mundane persons. </div> </div> </div>Requiting it's done on a need to know basis, the majority of the members don't need to know they're members. Members are shown undeniable proof. Besides, the Technocracy it's part of it (which I think it's wrong, Technocracy shouldn't trust so much in unaligned humans).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example - a stack of notes on the supernatural made by someone is enough to discredit them if it is publicized. Another one - the fact that mundane humans might become totally estranged and isolated from their loved ones and friends; because even if they attempt to tell them about the supernatural, they very often will meet with total disbelief. A person not coming back home increasingly often does not look good for a spouse or a best friend. Such a disrupted social life can of course be exploited by the Nightfolk. If they try to make up the lost time to their families and friends, then the new inquisition loses capabilities </div> </div> </div>IF I'm right, which I hope isn't the case, we're talking about all big governments and intelligence agencies here (+ Technocracy), not a random guy trying to publish a paper. But this won't be a problem because they don't seem to want the supernatural to be public. At least that's not the vive I got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-19-2017, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}